    Bug 2058538 - Store and read auth realms for Exchange requests. r=edicharry

    This patch:

    * adds code infrastructure to store and read arbitrary server properties
      to/from prefs
    * changes the Rust `Credentials` generation to fetch any known auth
      realm for the server from a pref
    * checks for realm names in `WWW-Authentication` response headers, such
      that if one is provided and it differs from the one we know, we store
      it and try again before asking the user for new credentials

    Tests servers already use a custom `test` realm when responding with
    `WWW-Authenticate` headers, so no manual testing should be required.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314955

